      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers near Bayou Macon used the waterway to haul cotton and other goods to river ports, making it a natural transportation route.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/kilbourne_louisiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kilbourne was formally incorporated as a village in 1954 under Louisiana's Lawrason Act, a statute that enabled rural communities to organize local governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilbourne%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village’s early growth relied on cotton plantations and timber harvesting, but its isolation limited rapid development until roads and mills were built.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
